WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.240
Across the misty highlands and rugged coastlines of Scotland,

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:07.040
rise ancient guardians of history,

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.760
castles that have stood for centuries,

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:13.520
watching silently as time unfolds.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:16.880
From the windswept battlements of Eilean Donan,

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:20.880
perched at the meeting point of three sea lochs,

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:23.440
to the towering might of Edinburgh Castle,

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.480
carved into the very rock it rests upon.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:30.560
These fortresses are more than stone and mortar.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:34.160
They are stories frozen in time.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:38.880
Each castle whispers legends of kings and clans,

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.280
betrayals and bravery.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:44.960
Stirling Castle, once the childhood home of Mary,

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:48.720
Queen of Scots, echoes with royal footsteps.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:52.960
Urquhart Castle, gazing out over the dark waters of Loch Ness,

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.760
conjures tales of mythical beasts and long-lost battles.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:01.280
Some lie in ruins, romantic and haunting.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:05.600
Others, restored, invite travellers to walk their halls,

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:10.960
climb their towers, and feel the chill of history brush past.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:14.480
There are over 2,000 castles in Scotland,

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:19.520
each a chapter in a story of pride, power and peril.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:24.400
Every stone holds a secret, every gaze a ghost.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:29.440
This is Echoes of the Castle Keep.

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:32.800
[music]
